<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.4.0: Lesson Overview</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00108</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.4.0: Lesson Overview</md:title>
    <md:uuid>54888a0e-6493-4ebb-8608-d2842ff979af</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">In middle school, you learned that a solution to an equation is a value or values that make the equation true. In this lesson, you will revisit what you learned about solutions to equations in one variable and two variables. You will also continue to practice modeling relationships with equations and to make sense of equations and their solutions in context.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
      <list id="list-00001">
        <item>Explain what it means for a value or pair of values to be a solution to an equation.</item>
        <item>Find solutions to equations by reasoning about a situation or by using algebra.</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00003">Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
      <list id="list-00002">
        <item>1.4.1: Finding the Solution to an Equation in One Variable, Part 1</item>
        <item>1.4.2: Writing Equations to Represent Constraints<list id="list-00003">
            <item>1.4.2: Self Check</item>
            <item>1.4.2: Additional Resources</item>
          </list>
        </item>
        <item>1.4.3 Finding the Solution to an Equation in Two Variables<list id="list-00004">
            <item>1.4.3: Self Check</item>
            <item>1.4.3: Additional Resources</item>
          </list>
        </item>
        <item>1.4.4: Finding the Solution to an Equation in One Variable, Part 2</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00004">After that, you’ll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
      <list id="list-00005">
        <item>1.4.5: Practice</item>
        <item>1.4.6: Lesson Summary</item>
      </list>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>